17. Let $\boldsymbol{A} = \begin{pmatrix}2 & 6\\k & -1\end{pmatrix}$ and $\boldsymbol{B} = \begin{pmatrix}h & 3\\-3 & 7\end{pmatrix}$, where $h$ and $k$ are integers. Given that $\det\boldsymbol{A} = \det\boldsymbol{B}$ and that $\det\boldsymbol{AB} = 256h$,
(a) show that $h$ satisfies the equation $49h^2 - 130h + 81 = 0$;
(b) hence find the value of $k$.
